# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KiCAD
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Lock files created while a board/schematic is open (and left behind on crash)
*.lck
~*.lck
~*

# Auto-saves and backups
_autosave-*
*-backups/
*.kicad_pcb-bak
*.kicad_sch-bak
*.kicad_prl-bak
*.sch-bak
*.bak

# Per-user local project state: window layout, visible layers, last-used dialog
# settings. Not design data -- differs per machine and churns constantly.
# The shared settings live in *.kicad_pro, which IS committed.
*.kicad_prl

# Footprint/symbol caches, rebuilt automatically
fp-info-cache
sym-info-cache

# Generated reports and netlists
*.rpt
*-erc.rpt
*-drc.rpt
*.net

# Simulation / misc scratch
*.raw
*.ngspice

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated fabrication outputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hardware/output/ is deliberately COMMITTED: for a published hardware project
# the schematic PDF, BOM and Gerbers are the useful artifacts -- a reader can
# review the design or order boards without installing KiCAD.
#
# They are all regenerable from the .kicad_sch / .kicad_pcb, so if you would
# rather keep the repo lean and avoid churn on every re-route, uncomment:
#
# hardware/output/
